nU"␀5␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀HN␀␀u␀␀pâUS:X␀␀a␀␀US-␀␀nXì:º␀␀d␀␀XS:º␀␀a␀␀ ␀O6Xï:î␀␀a␀␀U	nM%␀␀UR␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Xï5␀␀␀␀␀␀(␀␀␀␀␀␀␀a␀␀SnUR␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Xï5␀␀␀␀␀␀ ␀MP␀␀␀ ␀U(␀␀␀␀␀␀␀d␀␀[␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀R␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"␀U5␀␀␀␀␀␀nU$␀s ␀snf␀)aˆ␀␀Read an undirected graph in sparse6 format from string.

Parameters
----------
string : string
   Data in sparse6 format

Returns
-------
G : Graph

Raises
------
NetworkXError
    If the string is unable to be parsed in sparse6 format

Examples
--------
>>> G = nx.from_sparse6_bytes(b":A_")
>>> sorted(G.edges())
[(0, 1), (0, 1), (0, 1)]

See Also
--------
read_sparse6, write_sparse6

References
----------
.. [1] Sparse6 specification
       <https://users.cecs.anu.edu.au/~bdm/data/formats.html>

